<title>BANGLADESH: Strike ends at Bangladesh port.</title>
<headline>Strike ends at Bangladesh port.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Bangladesh's main Chittagong port called off a strike on Thursday, a day after they walked out in protest over the recruitment of new employees, port officials said.</p>
<p>They said port authorities persuaded the strikers to return by assuring them that their share of the work on jetties and ships would not be affected by the new recruits.</p>
<p>The officials said the stoppage did not affect loading and unloading, but could have done so if goods and containers continued to pile up.</p>
<p>&quot;The stoppage has deprived the customs and port authorities of huge revenue,&quot; said one official before the strike was called off.</p>
</text>
